ime and commute-time machinery behind such bounds without a citation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Chandra Raghavan Ruzzo Smolensky Tiwari The electrical resistance of a graph captures its commute and cover times\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discussion ('Feature attribution and ceiling') and Conclusion propose resistance-based features motivated by the commute-time identity; no supporting reference exists in the draft or bibliography.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Matthews bounds on covering times of Markov chains via maximum hitting time and harmonic number\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The same Discussion and Conclusion passages cite Matthews-type bounds as the motivation for the richer-feature next step; the Matthews bound is also the basis of the unscored candidate mentioned in the supplementary model-selection note.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"query\": \"Hoerl Kennard Ridge regression: biased estimation for nonorthogonal problems\",\n      \"category\": \"core_method\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Related Work 'Statistical prediction with cheap features' and the Method's ridge estimator (needed because three features are collinear) carry no citation; a single classic reference grounds the model class the paper claims no novelty for.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"forbidden_query_patterns\": [\n    \"broader cover-time literatures for random regular or Erdős–Rényi graphs (deliberately not targeted by the gap artifact)\",\n    \"learned or deep-learning graph-property prediction (not supported by the draft)\",\n    \"re-retrieval of Feige upper/lower bounds or Kiwi et al., which are already in references.bib\",\n    \"queries about run chronology, attempts, or search history\"\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\nEOF\ncat > postdraft_reference_query_plan.md <<'EOF'\n# Post-draft reference query plan\n\n**Status:** ready. No retrieval was run in this stage.\n\n## Central topic\nRidge-regression 